    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires `checkDigit` to be a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`. I implemented it as a derived, read-only field following the existing conventions for other computed owner fields (`initials`, `membershipNumber`, `locality`, etc.):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (integer, 0\u20139), so the OpenAPI generator produces `checkDigit` on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`LuhnCheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 A plain static helper (mirroring the existing `MembershipLevel` helper) that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits contained in a string, ignoring non-digit characters. The algorithm matches the reference `luhn(...)` in the test exactly (rightmost digit doubled, alternating; subtract 9 when a doubled value exceeds 9; return the amount that rounds the sum up to the next multiple of ten).\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that derives `checkDigit` from `owner.getCustomerCode()` via `LuhnCheckDigit.forDigits(...)`, so it's computed on read like the other derived fields.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes, and the full test suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
